## What to deliver

Build and rig the forge up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a huge blocky masonry forge tower with a throat
up its center, a massive hammer riding in that throat, and a toothed gear crown
seated atop it. **Author the two required animations** as F-curves with the
`voxel-anim` animation subcommands: `hammer_stamp` (the great hammer dropping deep
down its throat and rising back to rest, landing with weight, not a weightless
slide) and `crown_spin` (the gear crown turning one steady full revolution and
looping seamlessly). Both are self-playing idles, so the forge cycles on its own
while the forge tower stays fixed. The animations are the fixed contract — produce
both, by those names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. You may add
your own extra parts, joints, or animations on top. When you are satisfied, stop:
the recorded per-part logs and `rig.json` are your finished submission.
